set_tab_title "hloth.dev/me/about"
printf '\033[1m%s\033[0m\n\033[2m%s\033[0m\n' '„Think different“' 'is my life slogan'
printf '\n%s\n' 'Thinking different was a choice I made early in life. As a kid, I often felt
two steps ahead of my classmates — and out of place because of it. While
others followed the curriculum, I was tinkering with computers, building my
first website at 9 and discovering my first security vulnerability in my
school’s IT system by 15. Instead of curiosity, I was met with suspicion.'
printf '\n%s\n' 'At school IT competitions, most participants showcased recycled ideas —
generic research, overused robots, or well-known solutions for unneeded
problems. I think different, so I always focused on creativity, innovation,
and real-world usefulness, surprising juries with modern technologies
outstanding from what they'\''re used to.'
printf '\n%s\n' 'At home, it wasn’t much different. My parents didn’t see value in my path
and pressured me to study. By 17, I moved into my own apartment to create
space for the future I believed in. People, whose whole goal in life is to
serve the country and have two kids, think that a progressive young boy
announcing he’s moving to Europe with his boyfriend is crazy. But I think
different.'
